  "maxPfDefinitionChange": {
    "resolved": "Settled, and the definition changed. The sheet and Sleeper disagreed for four teams because the sheet let a starting slot sit empty rather than start a negative score, while Sleeper always fields a full lineup. Max PF (calculated) is now \"best full lineup; every starting slot filled\", which reproduces Sleeper ppts for all 14 teams.",
    "cause": "The only negative scores in weeks 1-4 are four team defenses, each on a roster carrying no second DEF, so a full lineup had to absorb them. That is exactly the four teams and exactly the four deltas — which is why every gap was a whole number of points, the observation this block could not previously explain.",
    "refuted": "Slot-assignment order is not the cause, which was the earlier leading hypothesis. On this league's structure — dedicated slots plus a shared FLEX pool — greedy-by-slot, greedy-by-player and the exact DP return the same number for every team in every week.",
    "effect": "maxPfBestLegalLineup and pointsLeftOnBench each fell by the delta for these four teams; the other ten are unchanged. The sheet therefore showed 1-2 points more for them, and its old values are recorded below.",
    "reproduceOldNumbers": "optimalLineup(..., { allowEmptySlots: true }) returns the sheet's value for all 14 teams; asserted in packages/core/src/metrics/max-pf.investigate.test.ts.",
